id: q-space/node
title: "Q-Space"
kind: unresolved-question-view
status: owner-review-required
updated: 2026-08-14
protocol_revision: q-space.protocol.v1

governing_question: "What is Q-Space?"

answer: >
  Q-Space is the human-facing View of unresolved questions. It preserves
  attributed answers, candidate next questions, repeated Pattern candidates,
  state transitions, bounded probes, and proof without turning repetition or
  model output into truth.

responsibility_map:
  .yawn: portable public contracts
  YAWN.bot: first runtime and account boundary
  Supabase: private account-owned event ledger
  Q-Space: navigable View of that ledger
  YAWN.ai: optional intelligence adapter, never source of truth

routes:
  protocol: q-space/protocol-v1.yawn
  question_node: templates/q-space-question-node.yawn
  answer_event: templates/q-space-answer-event.yawn
  frontier_candidate: templates/q-space-frontier-candidate.yawn
  pattern_candidate: templates/q-space-pattern-candidate.yawn
  transition_event: templates/q-space-transition-event.yawn
  proof_event: templates/q-space-proof-event.yawn
  runtime: https://github.com/yawn-ai/web-game/tree/main/src/app/q-space

rules:
  - "Repeated answers may create a Pattern candidate; they never create truth or closure."
  - "A model may propose; only a human acceptance creates a durable next question."
  - "A question resolves only for a named purpose with proof and owner confirmation."
  - "Reopening appends a reopen event and preserves the prior resolution."
  - "Q-Space records bounded probe plans and results but executes no external action autonomously."

boundary:
  private_memory: excluded
  credentials: excluded
  production_runtime_state: excluded
  publication: owner-approval-required
